<section class="wrap narrow legal">
<div class="rv">
    <h2>Services</h2>
    <p>We provide Google Ads strategy, account structure, campaign setup, management, optimisation and reporting across the campaign types agreed with you in writing: Search, Shopping, Performance Max, YouTube, Display, Demand Gen, remarketing and Local Services Ads. The specific scope for your engagement is set out in your proposal, which takes precedence over this page.</p>

    <h2>Fees</h2>
    <p>Published pricing is $200 for a one-time account analysis, $999 per month for ad management, or 10% of managed ad spend for performance-based engagements. Fees are quoted exclusive of any applicable taxes and confirmed in your proposal before work begins.</p>
    <p><strong>Advertising spend is separate from our fees.</strong> You pay Google directly from your own Google Ads account using your own payment method. We never hold, invoice or mark up your advertising budget.</p>

    <h2>Payment</h2>
    <p>Management fees are payable monthly in advance. The account analysis is payable before delivery. Invoices are due within seven days. If payment is more than fourteen days late we may pause work on the account until it is settled.</p>

    <h2>Account ownership</h2>
    <p>Your Google Ads account is registered to your business and remains your property. Campaigns, audiences, ad copy, creative assets and tracking configurations produced during the engagement belong to you and stay with you if the engagement ends.</p>

    <h2>What we can and cannot promise</h2>
    <p>We commit to the standard of work described in your proposal: research, correct conversion tracking, structured testing, ongoing optimisation and honest reporting.</p>
    <p>We cannot guarantee specific results. Advertising performance depends on factors outside our control, including auction competition, platform policy and algorithm changes, your pricing and offer, your website's ability to convert, product availability, seasonality and your sales process. Any figures discussed in advance are estimates based on available data, not commitments.</p>
    <p>Google may change campaign types, bid strategies, reporting and policies at any time, and such changes can affect performance without notice.</p>

    <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Providing timely access to your Google Ads account, analytics and website.</li>
      <li>Ensuring your products, services and advertising claims comply with applicable law and Google Ads policies.</li>
      <li>Approving creative and copy where approval is required.</li>
      <li>Responding to leads and orders generated by campaigns.</li>
      <li>Maintaining a valid payment method on your Google Ads account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Google Ads policies</h2>
    <p>All campaigns are subject to Google Ads policies. Google may disapprove ads or products, or suspend accounts, at its discretion. We will work to resolve such issues but cannot control the outcome or timescale.</p>

    <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
    <p>Each party will keep the other's commercial information confidential and use it only for the purpose of the engagement.</p>

    <h2>Ending the engagement</h2>
    <p>Either party may end the engagement with fourteen days' written notice. On termination we hand over account access and any work in progress. Fees already paid cover the month in progress and are not refunded pro rata. No fee is charged for any month that has not started.</p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Our total liability in connection with the engagement is limited to the management fees you paid in the three months before the claim arose. We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, for lost profit or revenue, or for changes Google makes to its platform, policies, auction behaviour or pricing.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan, and the courts of Islamabad have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.</p>

    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy policy</h2>
    <p>digitalfadi is operated by Fawad Hussain as a sole trader based in Pakistan. For any question about your data, contact <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:22px">What we collect</h3>
    <p>Only what you actively send us. If you complete a form on this site: your name, business name, email address, website, and optionally your phone number, budget range, campaign goal, campaign type interests and message.</p>
    <p>This website uses Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics to measure how pages are used. These set cookies in your browser and send usage data, including your IP address, to Google. We use this only to understand which pages are read and where enquiries come from, never to identify you personally. You can block these cookies in your browser settings or with any standard blocker, and the site works normally without them. Fonts load from Google Fonts, which means your browser requests them from Google's servers and Google receives your IP address as part of that request.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:22px">Why we use it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>To reply to your enquiry and discuss whether we can help.</li>
      <li>To prepare a proposal or audit if you ask for one.</li>
      <li>To keep a record of business correspondence.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your details, share them for third-party marketing, or add you to a mailing list from an enquiry form. Newsletter subscription is separate and opt-in.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:22px">Where it goes and how long we keep it</h3>
    <p>Form submissions are processed by our hosting provider's form service and reach us by email. The site is hosted by Netlify, whose form service receives submissions and forwards them by email to a Google inbox. Both providers store data on servers in the United States and the European Union. Enquiries that don't become work are deleted after twelve months. Client records are kept for the duration of the relationship plus any period required for tax and accounting.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:22px">Your rights</h3>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, export or delete the information we hold about you, and to object to how we use it. Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we will respond within one month.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:22px">Client advertising accounts</h3>
    <p>When managing campaigns we work inside Google Ads accounts owned by our clients. Any end-user data collected there is governed by that client's own privacy policy and Google's terms, not this one.</p>

    <h2>Contact &amp; changes</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. If either section changes materially we will update the date here. Last updated 1 October 2026.</p>
  </div>
